00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.430
And the growth ranges
all over the place.

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:49.100
So I took the quintile,
the percentiles--

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:51.310
the 25th percentile,
the 50th percentile,

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:58.930
and the 75th percentile values
for some of these columns

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.630
and bucketized them so that--

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.630
because I don't care if
the growth is 40% or 50%.

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:06.040
That's roughly the same thing.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.660
So I want the model to
recognize it as such.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.840
I've done the same thing
here with headcount

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.820
and with revenue.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.350
And revenue is
especially notable

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:17.510
because the ranges are
all over the place.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:20.200
And so knowing where
the percentiles are

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.200
helps you get a nice, even
distribution of your data

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.220
across the buckets.

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:28.080
And so with all the
feature columns set up,

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.630
I made two different
models, a linear model

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.640
and a deep learning model.

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:35.863
So the linear model did
pretty good, I'd say,

00:18:35.863 --> 00:18:36.780
all things considered.

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:39.880
When I finished evaluating,
we came out to about 76%.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.880
My accuracy-- I could
keep training longer.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:44.640
I could keep banging my head
against the different features

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.260
and different columns,
add more data.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:50.732
But all things considered, given
that the [INAUDIBLE] piece here

00:18:50.732 --> 00:18:52.190
was when I first
started doing this

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:53.732
and I didn't have
any buckets at all,

00:18:53.732 --> 00:18:57.130
I was getting, like, 20% error
accuracy, which is terrible.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:19:00.210
So the changes really made
a meaningful difference.

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:03.330
And on the deep model side,
I just made a simple model.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.940
It's a three-layer
model with 20, 15,

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:09.960
and 10 neurons per layer,
so not terribly large,

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.520
not terribly sophisticated.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:15.420
But with that and training
for the same amount of time,

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.410
it got 86%.

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:18.790
So it's still not perfect.

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.460
I'm not looking for
perfection here,

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:23.920
